-- The stratification rejection fixture: a cycle THROUGH a negation.
--
-- `p holds` depends negatively on `q holds`, which depends negatively on
-- `p holds` — the Apt–Blair–Walker definition of unstratified. The shared
-- relational middle-end RECORDS this (jl4/examples/relational/unstratified.l4
-- lowers successfully and asserts on its `stratification:` block); the Blawx
-- leg REJECTS it in v1 with a named diagnostic, because its L4-oracle
-- determinism obligation cannot honour multiple stable models
-- (BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC R2 / #258 §2.5 division of labour).

DECLARE Flag HAS
    seed IS A BOOLEAN

@export
GIVEN f IS A Flag
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `p holds` IF
    f's seed AND NOT `q holds` f

@export
GIVEN f IS A Flag
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `q holds` IF
    NOT `p holds` f
